{"title":"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pyramid has a square base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  The area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f40cb7585c44d066022164abae4d42af57a926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$196$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, and the areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b984c55719cc5f992ee62656d920ac15c78d9137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791f15f656db201fa9116a2f762a4b292fc50883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, respectively.  What is the volume of the pyramid?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7316f6ff78d82e9a1b52715fad6b1ad6313a96e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 392 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 196\\sqrt {6} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 392\\sqrt {2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 392\\sqrt {3} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 784$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"512\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the height of the pyramid and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. The side length of the base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The heights of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b984c55719cc5f992ee62656d920ac15c78d9137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58e78619c8460f974cb76dc2bdf007646105b1ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot105\\div14=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"131\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cecebbd0513eb6998445216e7c4ffb4a8abd0ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot91\\div14=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. Consider a side view of the pyramid from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423d2cdb9f74980709bf26fc4bb3cb0304964a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />.  We have a systems of equations through the Pythagorean Theorem:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec32223f9131a1e6a64f3040f88e2c187e01c9ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^2-(14-a)^2=h^2 \\\\ 15^2-a^2=h^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"160\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Setting them equal to each other and simplifying gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca759116eabca3226d8e044136d946108ad00abd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-27+28a=225 \\implies a=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"225\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffe0a2cfe66fc0e58279344c7a979bb8d633231e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=\\sqrt{15^2-9^2}=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, and the volume of the pyramid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aabd3babd08b32028e707d45b1beb071c62cd3d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{bh}{3}=\\frac{12\\cdot 196}{3}=\\boxed{784 \\Rightarrow E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"216\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B\">2008 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016230145\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 209/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4235/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.215      1 -total\n 59.82%    8.504      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.71%    5.50